---
import PageSite from "@layouts/PageSite.astro";
import Hero from "@components/redesign/Hero.astro";
---

<PageSite title="Community" description="How StuyPulse gives back: robot demos, FLL mentoring and camps, and helping other FRC teams." image="/community/BPC_Demo.jpg" fullBleed>
  <Hero
    title="Giving back."
    intro="Our mission is to help students find their pulse for lifelong learning, through a team culture that shares knowledge and gives back to the community."
    photo="/community/BPC_Demo.jpg"
    photoAlt="A StuyPulse robot demo in Battery Park City for STEAM Day"
    stickers={["Demos", "FLL camps", "Since 2001"]}
  >
    <Fragment slot="actions">
      <a class="pill pill-white" href="#fll">FLL programs</a>
      <a class="pill pill-ghost" href="/resources">Resources for teams</a>
    </Fragment>
  </Hero>

  <section class="band split" aria-labelledby="school">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 id="school" class="band-title">At Stuyvesant</h2>
      <p>
        After our rookie year, Stuyvesant started an Intro to Robotics class, taught by our head coach and mentor, Joseph
        Blay. It's still open to juniors and seniors, and it got several other schools thinking about a course of their own.
      </p>
      <p>
        We demo robots at alumni reunions, giving tours of the lab and showing what we've built. At the 2025 Open House we
        showed Aunt Mary, our 2025 robot, to hundreds of incoming freshmen and their parents. We hope robotics becomes one of
        their reasons for choosing Stuy.
      </p>
    </div>
    <img src="/community/Open_House.jpg" alt="New students and parents at Stuyvesant's Open House looking at Aunt Mary" loading="lazy" />
  </section>

  <section class="band split reverse" aria-labelledby="demos">
    <img src="/community/BPC_Demo.jpg" alt="A robot demo at Battery Park City for STEAM Day" loading="lazy" />
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 id="demos" class="band-title">Demos and media</h2>
      <p>
        In February 2025 we were on the FRC Open Alliance show, explaining our robot's mechanisms, and FUN Robotics named us
        an FRC Team of the Week for our Open Alliance work. In summer 2025 we alpha-tested SystemCore and presented what we
        learned at NYC Robo Replay, StuySplash and the NYC FIRST Kickoff.
      </p>
      <p>
        We've demoed robots at the local senior center, where our members also volunteer to help older adults with tech. At
        the NYC FIRST STEM Center we showed our 2024 offseason robot to students visiting from Japan, and smaller robots to
        Pre-K through 5th graders.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fll" id="fll" aria-labelledby="fll-title">
    <h2 id="fll-title">FIRST LEGO League</h2>
    <p class="lead">
      Since 2001 we've helped younger students take their first steps into engineering through FLL. It's still one of the
      main ways we share STEM.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Williamsburg</b><span>An FLL Challenge program for the past three years</span></li>
      <li><b>Bensonhurst</b><span>SPIKE Prime summer camps, and four teams mentored</span></li>
      <li><b>Battery Park City</b><span>An FLL Explore team, three years running</span></li>
      <li><b>Chinatown</b><span>SPIKE Prime summer camps for two years</span></li>
      <li><b>MoMath</b><span>A summer program in 2024</span></li>
      <li><b>Puerto Rico</b><span>Mentoring teams since 2018</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="lead">We also helped Queens team 4017, the RoboPandas, get ready for competition.</p>
    <div class="actions"><a class="pill pill-white" href="/resources/tutorials/fll">Our FLL curriculum</a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="band split" aria-labelledby="teams">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 id="teams" class="band-title">Helping other teams</h2>
      <p>
        We're always ready to help other teams, in build season or at competitions. We visit teams and invite them to our lab
        to share what we know about safety, organization, fundraising, engineering and software. At competitions we send
        members to help fix robots, and cheer when our friends win awards or reach the finals.
      </p>
      <p>Many of those teams have become lasting friends.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="pill pill-red" href="/resources">Resources for teams</a>
        <a class="pill pill-line" href="/resources/stuysplash">StuySplash</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <img src="/community/Stuy_Balta.jpg" alt="Team BALTA visiting the Stuyvesant robotics lab" loading="lazy" />
  </section>
</PageSite>

<style>
  .split {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr;
    gap: clamp(28px, 5vw, 72px);
    align-items: center;
  }
  .split + .split {
    padding-top: 0;
  }
  .split.reverse {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.1fr;
  }
  .split h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .split img {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 3;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }
  .fll {
    margin: 0 20px;
    padding: clamp(56px, 7vw, 96px) var(--gutter);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: var(--red);
    color: #fff;
  }
  .fll h2 {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 4.4rem);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: 19px;
    max-width: 56ch;
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    opacity: 0.94;
  }
  .fll ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 40px 0 28px;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(240px, 1fr));
    gap: 14px;
  }
  .fll li {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
    padding: 22px 26px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: #fff;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .fll li b {
    color: var(--red);
    font-size: 21px;
  }
  .fll li span {
    color: var(--soft);
    font-size: 16px;
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .split,
    .split.reverse {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .split.reverse img {
      order: 1;
    }
    .fll {
      margin: 0 12px;
    }
  }
</style>
